     "content": "**Yes, you should take it.** \n\nThis is a major win. By holding firm on your unvested equity, you successfully extracted **$205,000 in additional guaranteed cash** ($5,000 base bump + $200,000 sign-on bonus). \n\nAt this point, you have reached the upper boundary of what Google will authorize for an external L6 PM without a competing offer letter in hand. Pushing further would offer diminishing returns and risk souring the relationship.\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Updated Numbers Breakdown\n\nYour Year 1 compensation has shifted from a modest ~5\u201310% bump to a **massive ~44%+ increase** over Meta:\n\n| Component | Current Meta (IC6) | Revised Google Offer (L6) | Delta |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Base Salary** | $240,000 | **$240,000** | $0 (Base matched) |\n| **Target Bonus** | 15% (~$36,000) | 20% (**$48,000**) | +$12,000 |\n| **New-Hire RSUs (Yr 1)** | ~$200,000\u2013$250,000 | **$270,000** *(flat)* or **$356k+** *(if frontloaded)* | +$20,000 to +$106,000 |\n| **Sign-on Bonus** | $0 | **$200,000** | +$200,000 (Guaranteed cash) |\n| **Year 1 Total Comp** | **~$526,000** | **~$758,000 \u2013 $844,000+** | **+$232,000 to +$318,000** |\n\n* **4-Year Baseline Average (without refreshers):** ~$608,000/year (vs. ~$526k at Meta).\n* **4-Year Average (with standard ~$250k/yr refreshers):** **~$700,000+/year.**\n\n---\n\n### 2. Why This is the Right Time to Sign\n\n1. **They fully covered your transition risk in cash:** Most candidates have to fight to get forfeited unvested stock matched via additional equity (which carries market volatility and vesting cliff risks). Google gave you **$200,000 in liquid, guaranteed cash upfront**.\n2. **Top-tier calibration for L6:** An L6 PM package delivering ~$758k+ Year 1 and a ~$1.08M initial grant puts you comfortably in the **90th+ percentile** for Google L6 PM offers.\n3. **No further leverage required:** Because you didn't have an active competing offer from another company, extracting a $200k sign-on strictly using your Meta unvested stock as an anchor was the maximum realistic outcome.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Checklist of Final Details to Confirm\n\nBefore you sign the final paperwork, verify these three administrative points with your recruiter:\n\n1. **Sign-on Payout & Clawback Terms:**\n   * Confirm if the $200,000 is paid as a **single lump sum** within your first 30\u201360 days, or split across two years (e.g., $100k Year 1 / $100k Year 2).\n   * Check the clawback period (standard is a 1-year pro-rated repayment if you leave voluntarily).\n2. **Equity Vesting Cadence:**\n   * Clarify whether it is flat (25%/25%/25%/25%) or Google's front-loaded schedule (e.g., 33%/33%/22%/12% or 38%/32%/20%/10%), and whether it vests monthly or quarterly after an initial cliff.\n3. **Start Date Flexibility:**\n   * Pick a start date that allows you to collect any pending Meta bonus or immediate stock vest if you are within a few weeks of one.\n\n---\n\n### 4. How to Accept Gracefully\n\n> *\"Hi [Recruiter Name],*\n>\n> *Thank you for working with the compensation committee to put this together. I really appreciate you addressing my unvested equity and bringing the base to $240,000 with the $200,000 sign-on bonus.*\n>\n> *This bridges the gap, and I\u2019m excited to accept. Please send over the revised written offer and let me know the next steps for background check and selecting a start date.\"*",
